So for a same-repo PR, head.repo exists and equals the base repo, so `ghPrHeadRepoFull` returns the base's own full name. The doc comment "(null when the REST body carries no head.repo (deleted fork) or it IS the base: both keep the base-reprobe behavior downstream)" — the caller (`isDeadHeadParked`) passes headFull but `_ghBranchExistsRef` checks `!(parts[0] === owner && parts[1] === repo)` and keeps the base probe when it names the base. OK.

So a `crossRepo` guard: `item.headRepo` (from the PR list payload, resolved by `_prItemFromPr` via `smProviderModule.ghPrHeadRepoFull(p)`) differs from the base `owner + '/' + repo`. For a fork PR: headRepo = 'forkowner/reponame' ≠ base. For same-repo: equals base. For a deleted fork: null → treat as not cross-repo (fail closed).

