Hmm — wait. The GC rule with query type pr + branchPrefix would match OPEN guest PRs (transplant PRs in flight) and call a gc action on them — the gc action must check the PR state: OPEN → nothing. Closed ones aren't in the open list... So a query-driven GC can't find closed PRs. So GC must be the sweep-from-refs design executed once per tick at rule level, not per-item. 

